HST PDF: the viewer cannot be closed under its own print dialog.

The viewer prints asynchronously (Printer::PrintJob posts the job; the print dialog runs from a
user event) and the print controller keeps the viewer's document and its window as the dialog
parent. A close() of the viewer's frame while the dialog was open, from another thread (UNO
automation), disposed both under the running dialog; when the dialog returned, the print code
wrote through the destroyed window and the office died (exit 255: its own crash handler faulted
as well, no Windows dump).

Windows r1-auto W12 failed this way in every run: the check never found the print dialog (UI
Automation lists it under its owner window), so it closed the viewer with the dialog still open.
A probe that closes the viewer over UNO with the dialog open crashed at 100% and 150% (ProcDump
full dumps, run 42963658080: main thread PrintJobAsync -> Printer::ImplPrintJob, access
violation writing address 0x1c0 after the dialog; office exit 255).

The print controller now holds an action lock on the viewer's frame from the print command to
the end of the job. A close() meanwhile is refused with a CloseVetoException (as for a frame that
is loading); with ownership delivered the frame closes itself when the lock is released. The lock
is released from a user event, after the print code has unwound.

